{"name":"High Society","hex":"#cab7c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"high society","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The socially interacting wealthy fashionable elite of a society, especially in Western societies."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/high_society"}],"entries":[{"title":"High Society (1924 film)","blocks":[{"text":"High Society is a 1924 American short silent comedy film directed by Robert F. McGowan. It was the 29th Our Gang short subject to be released."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Our_Gang_High_Society_title_card.jpg/330px-Our_Gang_High_Society_title_card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Society_(1924_film)","wikidata":"Q16251335"},{"title":"High Society (1932 film)","blocks":[{"text":"High Society is a 1932 British comedy film directed by John Rawlins and starring Florence Desmond, William Austin and Emily Fitzroy."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Society_(1932_film)","wikidata":"Q107026910"},{"title":"High Society (1956 film)","blocks":[{"text":"High Society is a 1956 American musical romantic comedy film directed by Charles Walters and starring Bing Crosby, Grace Kelly, and Frank Sinatra. The film was produced by Sol C. Siegel for Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, and shot in VistaVision and Technicolor, with music and lyrics by Cole Porter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/High_Society_%281956_film_poster%29.png/330px-High_Society_%281956_film_poster%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Society_(1956_film)","wikidata":"Q719471"},{"title":"High society","blocks":[{"text":"High society, sometimes simply Society, is the behavior and lifestyle of people with the highest levels of wealth, power, fame and social status. It includes their related affiliations, social events and practices. Upscale social clubs were open to men based on assessments of their ranking and role within high society. In American high society, the Social Register was traditionally a key resource for identifying qualified members. For a global perspective, see upper class. The quality of housing, clothing, servants and dining were visible marks of membership."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Caroline_Astor_and_her_guest%2C_New_York_1902.jpg/330px-Caroline_Astor_and_her_guest%2C_New_York_1902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_society","wikidata":"Q2910239"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Charles_Walters_Frank_Sinatra_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_High_Society_1956.jpg/500px-Charles_Walters_Frank_Sinatra_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_High_Society_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Charles_Walters_Frank_Sinatra_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_High_Society_1956.jpg/500px-Charles_Walters_Frank_Sinatra_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_High_Society_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"L–R: Director Charles Walters, Frank Sinatra, and Grace Kelly","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACharles_Walters_Frank_Sinatra_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_High_Society_1956.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Louis_Armstrong_and_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_%22High_Society%22%2C_1956.jpg/500px-Louis_Armstrong_and_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_%22High_Society%22%2C_1956.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Louis_Armstrong_and_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_%22High_Society%22%2C_1956.jpg/1280px-Louis_Armstrong_and_Grace_Kelly_on_the_set_of_%22High_S